// Program metadata for zsh.
//
// kind=user → installed by the profile runner inside the chroot as the owning
// user via paru, with temp NOPASSWD sudo for: refreshing the pkgfile database
// (`pkgfile -u`, root-owned /var/cache/pkgfile) and seeding /etc/skel so users
// created outside the dotfiles clone still get the shell tooling defaults.
// The zsh binary and login shell are NOT set here — User Core's shell=/bin/zsh
// + ensure_login_shell_installed already own that. This installs the
// interactive tooling the stowed config expects (eza/zoxide/fzf/nvm/…),
// pre-warms the zinit plugin cache so the first login shell clones nothing, and
// seeds the Noctalia-generated theme files (Catppuccin Mocha Sapphire default).

{
  "name": "zsh",
  "kind": "user",
  "description": "Interactive zsh tooling (eza, zoxide, fzf, nvm, p10k deps) with a pre-warmed zinit cache and seeded palette theme.",
  "system_services": ["pkgfile-update.timer"]
}
